
<%args>
$trial_id
$trial_stock_type
</%args>

<& /util/import_javascript.mas, classes => [ 'CXGN.List' ], entries => [ 'trial_accession_change' ] &>

% my $title = '';
% if ($trial_stock_type eq 'cross') {
%    $title = 'Change Cross Unique IDs or Accessions';
% } elsif ($trial_stock_type eq 'family_name') {
%    $title = 'Change Family Names or Accessions';
% } else {
%    $title = 'Change Accessions';
% }


<div class="modal fade" id="trial_design_change_accessions_dialog" name="trial_design_change_accessions_dialog" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="trialDesignChangeAccessionsDialog">
    <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header" style="text-align: center">
                <button type="button" class="close" data-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"><span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span></button>
                <h4 class="modal-title" id="trialDesignChangeAccessionsDialog"><%$title%></h4>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">
                <div class="container-fluid">

                    <div class="well well-sm">
                        <p><b>Correct the trial with a file of what was planted:</b></p>
                        <ol style="padding-left: 20px">
                            <li><a class="btn btn-default btn-sm" id="trial_design_change_accessions_download" href="/breeders/trial/<% $trial_id %>/download/layout?format=xlsx&amp;dataLevel=plots&amp;selected_columns=%7B%22plot_name%22%3A1%2C%22accession_name%22%3A1%2C%22plot_number%22%3A1%2C%22block_number%22%3A1%2C%22rep_number%22%3A1%2C%22row_number%22%3A1%2C%22col_number%22%3A1%2C%22seedlot_name%22%3A1%7D">Download the current layout</a> (by plot number), or <b>Download Plot Order</b> with the planting order and borders in Field Layout Tools (for a trial with row and column numbers).</li>
                            <li>Write what was planted: change accession_name where another accession grows. In a file in planting order, a shift is a cut and paste of accession_name one row down; leave the border rows as they are.</li>
                            <li>Upload the file here, as .xlsx or as CSV with commas (a CSV that Excel saved with semicolons is not read). You see what changes before anything is changed. Plots that already match the file are left as they are, so the same file can be uploaded again while the plot names are kept, and a later correction starts from a new download. The file is kept with the trial (Uploaded Additional Files). Once the trial has phenotypes or seedlots, a curator uploads the file.</li>
                        </ol>
                        <p>Seed transactions follow the packets: a plot that got the packet of another plot takes over its seedlot. A packet that is in no plot any more (for example planted into a border) stays taken from its seedlot; if the seed of a place left empty went back into the seedlot, add it there. After the change, print new labels for the changed plots, and download new Field Book files and phenotyping spreadsheets.</p>
                        <& /help/file_upload_type.mas, type => "Accession exchanges", optional_column => 1 &>
                        <br/>

                        <div class="panel panel-default">
                            <div class="panel-body">
                                <b>Header:</b><br>
                                The first row (header) must contain the columns 'plot_name' and 'accession_name' or 'cross_unique_id' or 'family_name', depending on the stock type in this trial.<br>
                                An optional additional column, 'new_plot_name' can be added to change the plot names; the current name keeps it.<br>
                                Without a new name, the old name is replaced where it is a whole part of the plot name, or, if a plot name template has been saved in association with this trial, the template is used to rename the plot. Check "Keep the plot names" to keep all names.<br>
                                The file can list every plot of the trial, for example the plan as it was planted; plots whose accession does not change are left as they are. Other columns are ignored, and so are rows of a planting order file whose type is not plot (borders and gaps).<br>
                                An optional column 'seedlot_name' names the seedlot a plot was planted from, where it is not the one the plot has now; seed transactions follow the packets without it.<br>

                                <table style="margin-top: 3%;" class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                                  <tbody>
                                  <tr>
                                    <td>plot_name</td>
                                    <td>accession_name</td>
                                    <td>new_plot_name (optional)</td>
                                    <td>seedlot_name (optional)</td>
                                  </tr>
                                  </tbody>
                                </table>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <b>Required columns:</b><br>
                        <b>plot_name:</b> name of plot to change the accession for<br>
                        <b>accession_name or cross_unique_id or family_name:</b> name of the accession or cross unique id or family name that the plot should be connected to.<br>
                        <br><b>Optional columns:</b><br>
                        <b>new_plot_name:</b> new name for plot.<br>
                        <b>seedlot_name:</b> the seedlot the plot was planted from, where it is another one than now (a plot without a seed transaction gets one with Upload Seedlots Planted In Trial).<br>
                        <div class="list-group-item-warning" >
                          <p><i>Warning: the new plot name will replace the old plot name in subplots, plants, and tissue samples if possible. Plot numbers, blocks and, except in completely randomized designs, replicates are kept; check plots follow their accessions. Phenotypes stay with their plots. You may need to reprint labels after the changes are applied.</i></p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <form class="form-horizontal" method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data" encoding="multipart/form-data" id="trial_design_change_accessions_form" name="trial_design_change_accessions_form">
                        <div class="form-group">
                            <label class="col-sm-3 control-label">Upload File: </label>
                            <div class="col-sm-9" >
                                <input type="file" name="trial_design_change_accessions_file" id="trial_design_change_accessions_file" encoding="multipart/form-data" />
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="form-group">
                            <div class="col-sm-offset-3 col-sm-9">
                                <div class="checkbox"><label><input type="checkbox" name="keep_plot_names" id="trial_design_change_accessions_keep_names" value="1" checked /> Keep the plot names</label></div>
                                <p class="help-block" style="white-space: normal">Keep them while labels with the names are in the field or data was collected with them. Unchecked, plot names that contain the old accession name, or that follow the plot name template of the trial, are updated.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </form>

                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-footer">
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="trial_design_change_accessions_submit" >Submit</button>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-default" data-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="modal  fade" id="trial_design_replace_accessions_dialog_message" name="trial_design_replace_accessions_dialog_message" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="tDDialog">
    <div class="modal-dialog " role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header" style="text-align: center">
                <button type="button" class="close" data-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"><span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span></button>
                <h4 class="modal-title" id="tDDialog"><b><%$title%></b></h4>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">
                <div class="container-fluid">

                    <p3> The trial was changed:</p3>
                    <ul id="trial_design_change_accessions_summary"></ul>
                    <p>The plots that changed, for new labels (Label Designer) and new files:</p>
                    <textarea id="trial_design_changed_plots" class="form-control" rows="4" readonly></textarea>
                    <div id="trial_design_changed_plots_to_list" style="margin-top: 5px"></div>

                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-footer">
                <button id="close_replace_accession_dialog" type="button" class="btn btn-default" data-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>


<script>

jQuery(document).ready(function () {

    jQuery('#trial_detail_page_change_accessions').click(function(){
        jQuery('#trial_design_change_accessions_dialog').modal('show');
    });

    // the page shows the trial as it was; however the result is closed, show it as it is now
    jQuery('#trial_design_replace_accessions_dialog_message').on('hidden.bs.modal', function() {
        location.reload();
    });

    // the file is posted twice: first for the plan (preview), then, once the user agrees, to change the trial
    jQuery('#trial_design_change_accessions_submit').click(async function() {
        if (jQuery("#trial_design_change_accessions_file").val() === '') {
            alert("Please select a file");
            return;
        }
        var change = window.jsMod['trial_accession_change'];
        var summary = await change.changeWithPreview('/ajax/breeders/trial/<% $trial_id %>/change_plot_accessions_using_file/check', new FormData(jQuery('#trial_design_change_accessions_form')[0]), {
            title: "<% $title %>",
            alert: function(message, error) {
                return change.confirmDialog(change.plainText(error), { title: "<% $title %>", ok: "OK", cancel: null });
            },
            inform: function(message) {
                return change.confirmDialog(message, { title: "<% $title %>", ok: "OK", cancel: null });
            },
        });
        if (summary) {
            change.showSummary('#trial_design_change_accessions_summary', summary, false);
            jQuery('#trial_design_changed_plots').val(change.changedPlots(summary).join("\n"));
            if (typeof addToListMenu === 'function') {
                addToListMenu('trial_design_changed_plots_to_list', 'trial_design_changed_plots', { listType: 'plots' });
            }
            // after Bootstrap has closed this dialog, or the page under the next one scrolls with it
            jQuery('#trial_design_change_accessions_dialog').one('hidden.bs.modal', function() {
                jQuery('#trial_design_replace_accessions_dialog_message').modal("show");
            }).modal("hide");
        }
    });

});

</script>
